femto patch for quireink-stardict 0.3.0
Subject: validate dictzip header, chunk table, footer and chunk sizes

- Reject gzip headers with reserved flag bits set.
- Check the RA subfield: version 1, non-zero chunk length and count, table
  length matching the count, no empty chunks.
- Bound the optional name/comment header strings to 16 KiB.
- Read the gzip footer; require the compressed payload to fit in the file
  and the uncompressed size (ISIZE) to agree with the chunk count.
- Reads must lie inside the declared uncompressed size; offset arithmetic is
  checked.
- Every selected chunk is inflated completely and must produce exactly its
  declared size (the sink can no longer stop inflation early).

The gzip CRC is still not verified.

The test fixture generator (tests/lookup.rs) is changed to match what real
dictzip files look like and what the checks now require: one deflate stream
with a full flush per chunk, followed by a gzip trailer. It uses flate2 and
crc32fast as new dev-dependencies (pinned in the normalised Cargo.toml;
Cargo.toml.orig is not touched, matching the vendored tree).

